#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:97
msgid ""
"This document uses the following \"size encoding\" of non-negative integers: "
"From each byte, the seven least significant bits are used to form the "
"resulting integer. As long as the most significant bit is 1, this process "
"continues; the byte with MSB 0 provides the last seven bits.  The seven-bit "
"chunks are concatenated. Later values are more significant."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:100
msgid ""
"This size encoding should not be confused with the \"offset encoding\", "
"which is also used in this document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deltified representation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:107
msgid ""
"Conceptually there are only four object types: commit, tree, tag and "
"blob. However to save space, an object could be stored as a \"delta\" of "
"another \"base\" object. These representations are assigned new types "
"ofs-delta and ref-delta, which is only valid in a pack file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:113
msgid ""
"Both ofs-delta and ref-delta store the \"delta\" to be applied to another "
"object (called 'base object') to reconstruct the object. The difference "
"between them is, ref-delta directly encodes base object name. If the base "
"object is in the same pack, ofs-delta encodes the offset of the base object "
"in the pack instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:118
msgid ""
"The base object could also be deltified if it's in the same pack.  Ref-delta "
"can also refer to an object outside the pack (i.e. the so-called \"thin "
"pack\"). When stored on disk however, the pack should be self contained to "
"avoid cyclic dependency."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:129
msgid ""
"The delta data starts with the size of the base object and the size of the "
"object to be reconstructed. These sizes are encoded using the size encoding "
"from above.  The remainder of the delta data is a sequence of instructions "
"to reconstruct the object from the base object. If the base object is "
"deltified, it must be converted to canonical form first. Each instruction "
"appends more and more data to the target object until it's complete. There "
"are two supported instructions so far: one for copying a byte range from the "
"source object and one for inserting new data embedded in the instruction "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:133
msgid ""
"Each instruction has variable length. Instruction type is determined by the "
"seventh bit of the first octet. The following diagrams follow the convention "
"in RFC 1951 (Deflate compressed data format)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction to copy from base object"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  "
"+----------+---------+---------+---------+---------+-------+-------+-------+\n"
"  | 1xxxxxxx | offset1 | offset2 | offset3 | offset4 | size1 | size2 | size3 "
"|\n"
"  "
"+----------+---------+---------+---------+---------+-------+-------+-------+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:143
msgid ""
"This is the instruction format to copy a byte range from the source "
"object. It encodes the offset to copy from and the number of bytes to "
"copy. Offset and size are in little-endian order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:149
msgid ""
"All offset and size bytes are optional. This is to reduce the instruction "
"size when encoding small offsets or sizes. The first seven bits in the first "
"octet determine which of the next seven octets is present. If bit zero is "
"set, offset1 is present. If bit one is set offset2 is present and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:154
msgid ""
"Note that a more compact instruction does not change offset and size "
"encoding. For example, if only offset2 is omitted like below, offset3 still "
"contains bits 16-23. It does not become offset2 and contains bits 8-15 even "
"if it's right next to offset1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:158
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  +----------+---------+---------+\n"
"  | 10000101 | offset1 | offset3 |\n"
"  +----------+---------+---------+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:163
msgid ""
"In its most compact form, this instruction only takes up one byte (0x80) "
"with both offset and size omitted, which will have default values "
"zero. There is another exception: size zero is automatically converted to "
"0x10000."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction to add new data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:169
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  +----------+============+\n"
"  | 0xxxxxxx |    data    |\n"
"  +----------+============+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:174
msgid ""
"This is the instruction to construct the target object without the base "
"object. The following data is appended to the target object. The first seven "
"bits of the first octet determine the size of data in bytes. The size must "
"be non-zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reserved instruction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:180
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  +----------+============\n"
"  | 00000000 |\n"
"  +----------+============\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:182
msgid "This is the instruction reserved for future expansion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "Original (version 1) pack-*.idx files have the following format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:190
msgid ""
"The header consists of 256 4-byte network byte order integers.  N-th entry "
"of this table records the number of objects in the corresponding pack, the "
"first byte of whose object name is less than or equal to N.  This is called "
"the 'first-level fan-out' table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:192
msgid ""
"The header is followed by sorted 24-byte entries, one entry per object in "
"the pack.  Each entry is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:196
msgid ""
"4-byte network byte order integer, recording where the object is stored in "
"the packfile as the offset from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:197
msgid "one object name of the appropriate size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:198
msgid "The file is concluded with a trailer:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:201
msgid "A copy of the pack checksum at the end of the corresponding packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:203
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:304
msgid "Index checksum of all of the above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pack Idx file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:239
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        --  +--------------------------------+\n"
"fanout      | fanout[0] = 2 (for example)    |-.\n"
"table       +--------------------------------+ |\n"
"            | fanout[1]                      | |\n"
"            +--------------------------------+ |\n"
"            | fanout[2]                      | |\n"
"            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ |\n"
"            | fanout[255] = total objects    |---.\n"
"        --  +--------------------------------+ | |\n"
"main        | offset                         | | |\n"
"index       | object name 00XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX | | |\n"
"table       +--------------------------------+ | |\n"
"            | offset                         | | |\n"
"            | object name 00XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX | | |\n"
"            +--------------------------------+<+ |\n"
"          .-| offset                         |   |\n"
"          | | object name 01XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX |   |\n"
"          | +--------------------------------+   |\n"
"          | | offset                         |   |\n"
"          | | object name 01XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX |   |\n"
"          | ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   |\n"
"          | | offset                         |   |\n"
"          | | object name FFXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX |   |\n"
"        --| +--------------------------------+<--+\n"
"trailer   | | packfile checksum              |\n"
"          | +--------------------------------+\n"
"          | | idxfile checksum               |\n"
"          | +--------------------------------+\n"
"          .-------.\n"
"                  |\n"
"Pack file entry: <+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:243
msgid "packed object header:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:244
#, no-wrap
msgid "byte size extension bit (MSB)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:246
msgid "type (next 3 bit)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:247
msgid "size0 (lower 4-bit)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:251
msgid ""
"n-byte sizeN (as long as MSB is set, each 7-bit)  size0..sizeN form "
"4+7+7+..+7 bit integer, size0 is the least significant part, and sizeN is "
"the most significant part."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:251
#, no-wrap
msgid "packed object data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:254
msgid ""
"If it is not DELTA, then deflated bytes (the size above is the size before "
"compression)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:256
msgid ""
"If it is REF_DELTA, then base object name (the size above is the size of the "
"delta data that follows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:257
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:263
msgid "delta data, deflated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:262
msgid ""
"If it is OFS_DELTA, then n-byte offset (see below) interpreted as a negative "
"offset from the type-byte of the header of the ofs-delta entry (the size "
"above is the size of the delta data that follows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:263
#, no-wrap
msgid "offset encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:269
msgid ""
"n bytes with MSB set in all but the last one.  The offset is then the number "
"constructed by concatenating the lower 7 bit of each byte, and for n >= 2 "
"adding 2^7 + 2^14 + ... + 2^(7*(n-1))  to the result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:270
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Version 2 pack-*.idx files support packs larger than 4 GiB, and have some "
"other reorganizations. They have the format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:274
msgid "A 4-byte magic number '\\377tOc' which is an unreasonable fanout[0] value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:276
msgid "A 4-byte version number (= 2)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:278
msgid "A 256-entry fan-out table just like v1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:282
msgid ""
"A table of sorted object names.  These are packed together without offset "
"values to reduce the cache footprint of the binary search for a specific "
"object name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:287
msgid ""
"A table of 4-byte CRC32 values of the packed object data.  This is new in v2 "
"so compressed data can be copied directly from pack to pack during repacking "
"without undetected data corruption."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:292
msgid ""
"A table of 4-byte offset values (in network byte order).  These are usually "
"31-bit pack file offsets, but large offsets are encoded as an index into the "
"next table with the msbit set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:297
msgid ""
"A table of 8-byte offset entries (empty for pack files less than 2 GiB).  "
"Pack files are organized with heavily used objects toward the front, so most "
"object references should not need to refer to this table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:299
msgid "The same trailer as a v1 pack file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:302
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A copy of the pack checksum at the end of the\n"
"corresponding packfile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:305
#, no-wrap
msgid "pack-*.rev files have the format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:308
msgid "A 4-byte magic number '0x52494458' ('RIDX')."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:310
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:330
msgid "A 4-byte version identifier (= 1)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:312
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:332
msgid "A 4-byte hash function identifier (= 1 for SHA-1, 2 for SHA-256)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:316
msgid ""
"A table of index positions (one per packed object, num_objects in total, "
"each a 4-byte unsigned integer in network order), sorted by their "
"corresponding offsets in the packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:320
msgid ""
"A trailer, containing a checksum of the corresponding packfile, and a "
"checksum of all of the above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:322
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:352
msgid "All 4-byte numbers are in network order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:323
#, no-wrap
msgid "pack-*.mtimes files have the format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:326
msgid "All 4-byte numbers are in network byte order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:328
msgid "A 4-byte magic number '0x4d544d45' ('MTME')."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:337
msgid ""
"A table of 4-byte unsigned integers. The ith value is the modification time "
"(mtime) of the ith object in the corresponding pack by lexicographic (index) "
"order. The mtimes count standard epoch seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:341
msgid ""
"A trailer, containing a checksum of the corresponding packfile, and a "
"checksum of all of the above (each having length according to the specified "
"hash function)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:342
#, no-wrap
msgid "multi-pack-index (MIDX) files have the following format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:345
msgid "The multi-pack-index files refer to multiple pack-files and loose objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitformat-pack.txt:350
msgid ""
"In order to allow extensions that add extra data to the MIDX, we organize "
"the body into \"chunks\" and provide a lookup table at the beginning of the "
"body. The header includes certain length values, such as the number of "
"packs, the number of base MIDX files, hash lengths and types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
